From b5abedbb524607d53231f45394ed37dd53c99b4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 00:56:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 198/638] feature_engagement: register desktop IPH on AROS
 [chromium] [aros]

Statement:
Chrome's desktop password and help surfaces reference the desktop in-product-help feature set, but AROS was absent from its declarations, definitions, registry, variations, and configurations.

Decision:
Admit AROS to the complete desktop IPH feature set instead of disabling individual call sites, preserving upstream help behavior and feature wiring.

Evidence:
The AROS cross build compiles feature_constants.o, feature_list.o, feature_configurations.o, and passwords_private_delegate_impl.o together after this change.

Chain:
; first native Chromium window; desktop feature completeness.
---
 .../public/feature_configurations.cc                   |  6 +++---
 .../feature_engagement/public/feature_constants.cc     |  5 +++--
 .../feature_engagement/public/feature_constants.h      |  5 +++--
 components/feature_engagement/public/feature_list.cc   |  5 +++--
 components/feature_engagement/public/feature_list.h    | 10 ++++++----
 5 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

